# A source on a new line after `take`, which takes no list: `;` stays certain.
mode: syntax
---- query
from t | take 5
from u | count
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..31
  PIPELINE@0..15
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    NAME_REF@5..6
      IDENT@5..6 "t"
    WHITESPACE@6..7 " "
    PIPE@7..8 "|"
    WHITESPACE@8..9 " "
    TAKE_OP@9..15
      IDENT@9..13 "take"
      WHITESPACE@13..14 " "
      LITERAL@14..15
        LONG@14..15 "5"
  WHITESPACE@15..16 "\n"
  PIPELINE@16..30
    IDENT@16..20 "from"
    WHITESPACE@20..21 " "
    NAME_REF@21..22
      IDENT@21..22 "u"
    WHITESPACE@22..23 " "
    PIPE@23..24 "|"
    WHITESPACE@24..25 " "
    COUNT_OP@25..30
      IDENT@25..30 "count"
  WHITESPACE@30..31 "\n"

error[DS0106]: missing `;` between statements
  --> query:1:16
  |
1 | from t | take 5
  |                ^ expected `;` here
2 | from u | count
  | ---- a new statement starts here
  |
  = help: end the statement with `;`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from t | take 5;
    from u | count
which parses without errors
